diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 139dc38..728228b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,11 +5,18 @@ Exports stored reports.
 ## Usage
 
 ```sh
+# CSV (the default)
 python -m reportkit.export --output reports.csv
+python -m reportkit.export --format csv --output reports.csv
+
+# PDF (requires pandoc and a PDF engine on PATH)
+python -m reportkit.export --format pdf --output reports.pdf
 ```
 
-Only CSV output is reachable from the command line. `write_html` in
-`reportkit.export` shows the conversion path: it writes an intermediate CSV file
-and hands it to pandoc through the shared helpers in `reportkit.shellutils`,
-which is where quoting, command building, and temporary files are dealt with for
-every conversion.
+`--format` accepts `csv` or `pdf` and defaults to `csv`. `--output` is the
+destination path and defaults to `reports.csv` or `reports.pdf` to match the format.
+
+PDF export writes an intermediate CSV file to a private temporary file, hands it to
+pandoc through `reportkit.shellutils.run_tool` (an argument list, no shell, so paths
+need no quoting), and deletes the temporary file afterwards. `write_html` uses the
+same path.
